    content: `

## What Burgers Does Broast Sara Serve in Madinah

Broast Sara's burger menu sits alongside its broast and shawarma lines and runs from a 7 SAR Chicken Burger up to a 16 SAR Double Zinger Cheese Burger. The lineup exists because mixed groups at branches like Al Daheetha on Sakmah Ibn Abi Salamah Street rarely order the same thing, with some wanting broast, some shawarma, and some reaching for a burger.

The same sourcing standard that applies to the [Original Broast](/en/menu) applies to every burger patty and fillet. Every chicken used across the menu comes from local Saudi suppliers, has never been frozen, and is hand slaughtered daily using the Islamic halal method, with a Muslim slaughterer reciting Bismillah before each slaughter and ensuring complete blood drainage.

## Why a Broast Chain Also Runs a Burger Line

A burger at 7 SAR using fresh, never frozen local Saudi halal chicken sits on a different cost and quality base than most fast food burgers at that price in Saudi Arabia, where imported frozen chicken patties are standard.

The HACCP framework that governs the broast kitchen covers the burger line in the same way:

- Receiving temperature checks on incoming chicken
- Continuous cold storage monitoring
- Cooking to a minimum internal temperature of 74 degrees Celsius
- Documented separation between raw and cooked product

These protocols are set out in full on the [Food Safety Policy page](/en/legal/food-safety), which applies to every item on the menu, not only the broast line.

## The 7 SAR Entry Burgers: Chicken Burger and Meat Burger

The Chicken Burger (7 SAR) uses a fried chicken fillet in a toasted bun with fresh greens and house sauce. The coating is lighter than the zinger variant, closer to a standard fried chicken profile, and a freshly prepared fillet should crack cleanly on the outside while pulling apart in moist layers inside.

The Meat Burger (7 SAR) uses a grilled beef patty.

- Chicken Burger: 7 SAR
- Meat Burger: 7 SAR

Both work as standalone light meals or as additions to a table ordering from the broast side of the [Broast Sara Menu page](/en/menu).

## The 8 SAR Cheese Tier: Chicken Cheese Burger and Meat Cheese Burger

The Chicken Cheese Burger (8 SAR) and the Meat Cheese Burger (8 SAR) take the same fillet or patty, the same bun, and the same house sauce, and add a melted cheese layer.

### How the Cheese Changes the Texture

The melted cheese adds a fat layer that softens the contrast between the crisp fillet and the bun, producing a more uniform bite than the base burgers, where the crunch of the fillet is more immediate. For customers who prefer a richer, more cohesive bite over a strong textural contrast, the cheese tier is the better fit.

At 8 SAR, both items remain below the price of comparable cheese burgers at international chains in Madinah, while using a higher chicken sourcing standard.

## The 12 SAR Double Tier: Double Chicken Burger and Double Cheese Meat Burger

The Double Chicken Burger (12 SAR) stacks two fried chicken fillets, so the chicken becomes the dominant element of the burger rather than the bun, with two layers of crust and seasoned coating and compounded steam released when the burger is pressed together.

The Double Cheese Meat Burger (12 SAR) doubles both the beef patty and the cheese.

- Double Chicken Burger: 12 SAR
- Double Cheese Meat Burger: 12 SAR

The Double Cheese Meat Burger suits customers with higher appetite needs, such as travellers who have been on the road or workers coming off a physical shift near branches like Al Hijrah on Prince Sultan Ibn Abd Al Aziz Road.

## The Double Zinger Cheese Burger: Broast Sara's Top Tier Burger at 16 SAR

The Double Zinger Cheese Burger (16 SAR) is the highest priced item on the burger menu. Zinger refers to a spiced, crispy coated fillet where the seasoning sits in the coating itself rather than in the base marinade, producing heat that builds over several bites rather than hitting immediately.

Two zinger fillets are stacked with melted cheese and spicy mayonnaise between the layers, so the dominant flavour comes from the zinger coating rather than the sauce or cheese. International chains in Madinah sell comparable double zinger formats at 25 to 35 SAR, often using imported frozen chicken.

This is the item to order if heat is the priority. It is the most assertive item on the menu and the one most often photographed at the table.

## How to Order Broast Sara Burgers

Burgers can be ordered through HungerStation at branches that support it, by searching Broast Sara, which shows real time branch availability and estimated delivery time, or directly via WhatsApp at any of the 8 branches, which works well for group orders combining burgers with broast or shawarma.

Walk-in customers at all branches get burgers cooked to order, so allow a few minutes for the fillet to be prepared fresh. Operating hours vary by branch: Al Daheetha runs split hours from 12:30 PM to 3:30 PM and 6:30 PM to 3:30 AM, Imam Bukhari from 6:30 PM to 4:00 AM, Al Hijrah from 12:30 PM to 2:30 AM, Hil Bahr from 12:30 PM to 3:00 AM, Aljwazat from 12:30 PM to 4:00 AM, Al Juruf from 7:30 PM to 3:00 AM, and Yanbu from 11:00 AM to 4:00 AM. The Abiar Al Mashi branch is open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. Hours may be adjusted during Ramadan and Hajj season, so confirm with the branch directly before visiting outside standard hours.

For the full menu and branch list, see the [Broast Sara Menu page](/en/menu) and the [Broast Sara Locations page](/en/locations).
`,
